duplfile lists its current directory tree (open("ls -R", "p")) and reports the file names that occur in more than one directory, so its output is whatever directory it runs in: in the shared progs/ staging it read every other unit's fixtures and went stale whenever one was added (gcomp.fixtures and the skeleton.icn of headicon/newicon after the 09-25 ref; iconx and SCRIP agreed byte for byte on the 10-05 staging). It runs in a directory of its own holding only duplfile.fixtures, a three-level tree with three names repeated across directories and one unique, for the oracle and both SCRIP modes (Lon CEO-1474)
